{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1880 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "56b97b50f1d9ea16f48d4cfa71ba6662b4903f4a2df8f9829069aed877903040" :edb/db-before-t 1879 :edb/db-after-t 1880 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535192 50 #inst "2026-10-08T19:11:37.369Z" 13194139535192 true] [17592186171889 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336774 13194139535192 true] [17592186171889 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336781 13194139535192 true] [17592186172519 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535192 true] [17592186172519 1100 "Use Pascal's triangle to determine the value of $(\\frac{5}{4})$." 13194139535192 false] [17592186172519 1100 "Use Pascal's triangle to determine the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4}).$" 13194139535192 true] [17592186172519 1145 "To find the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $5$ and position $4$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe value located in row $5$ and position $4$ is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 2 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 3 &  & 3 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  & 1 &  & 4 &  & 6 &  & 4 &  & 1 \\\\  &  & 1 &  & 5 &  & 10 &  & 10 &  & 5 &  & 1 \\\\  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4})=5.$" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336774 1017 #edb/ref 17592186336775 13194139535192 true] [17592186336774 1089 "q-70307" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336774 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535192 true] [17592186336774 1100 "Determine the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{6}).$" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336774 1113 #uuid "077c732c-f40a-5a81-8fab-6738873b6464" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336774 1145 "The binomial coefficient $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=7$ and $r=6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{6}) & =\\frac{7!}{(7-6)!\\cdot 6!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6!}{1!\\cdot 6!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot \\cancel{6!}}{1\\cdot \\cancel{6!}} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336775 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336776 13194139535192 true] [17592186336775 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336777 13194139535192 true] [17592186336775 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336778 13194139535192 true] [17592186336775 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336779 13194139535192 true] [17592186336775 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336780 13194139535192 true] [17592186336775 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535192 true] [17592186336775 1041 "selection" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336775 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336777 13194139535192 true] [17592186336775 1110 #uuid "a87f4679-1131-5e52-83e3-fe60c7dc19e5" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336776 1034 "12" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336776 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535192 true] [17592186336776 1111 #uuid "249cb78e-5b68-58eb-a78c-d49edae20131" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336777 1034 "7" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336777 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535192 true] [17592186336777 1111 #uuid "888968b8-e65a-51dd-8f75-2b83a4c7c269" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336778 1034 "21" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336778 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535192 true] [17592186336778 1111 #uuid "57b0513f-ccaf-5d85-a461-c2396b53e628" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336779 1034 "14" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336779 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535192 true] [17592186336779 1111 #uuid "682df283-50d6-55ad-a59e-e4e9ab4876cd" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336780 1034 "42" 13194139535192 true] [17592186336780 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535192 true] [17592186336780 1111 #uuid "bcc7f4bb-5f12-50ba-8093-d6403531e4fe" 13194139